BT /F2 13.0 Tf 72 696 Td (2. Related Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 660 Td (Cross-lingual embeddings. Multilingual word embeddings such as MUSE and LASER project) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 644 Td (several languages into one space. However, they are static and do not adapt to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 628 Td (document context. Neural machine translation approaches treat the problem as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 612 Td (translation task and lose token-level interpretability. The transformer architecture) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 596 Td (proposed by Vaswani et al. provides the backbone for our encoder, while recent work on) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 580 Td (attention visualization motivates the interpretability analysis in Section 4.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.0 Tf 72 564 Td (Table 1: Benchmark datasets used in the experiments, with language pairs and average document length.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 72 532 Td (2.1 Transformer basics) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 496 Td (The transformer processes a sequence of tokens with self-attention layers, producing a) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 480 Td (contextual representation for every token. Each head computes queries, keys and values) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 464 Td (from the input, and the output is a weighted sum of the values. Multi-head attention) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 448 Td (allows the model to attend to different subspaces in parallel.) Tj ET
endstream
