BT /F2 13.0 Tf 72 696 Td (3. Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 660 Td (Our framework contains three components: a shared encoder, a token-level attention) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 644 Td (scorer and a prediction head. The encoder maps tokens of any supported language into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 628 Td (common representation space, and the scorer computes a relevance distribution over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 612 Td (source tokens for a given query. The final prediction is produced by the head from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 596 Td (attended representation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.0 Tf 72 580 Td (score\(q, k\) = q * k / sqrt\(d\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 72 548 Td (3.1 Model architecture) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 512 Td (The encoder is a 6-layer transformer with 8 attention heads and hidden size 512. We) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 496 Td (share all parameters across languages and train with a masked language modeling) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 480 Td (objective before fine-tuning on the downstream task. The attention scorer takes the) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 464 Td (query representation and the encoder outputs, and applies a bilinear score before) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 448 Td (softmax normalization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.0 Tf 72 432 Td (Figure 2: Training loss curves on the two benchmarks, showing convergence within 20 epochs.) Tj ET
endstream
