BT /F2 13.0 Tf 72 696 Td (4. Experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 660 Td (We evaluate on two multilingual benchmarks: XQuAD-R and MLQA-R. We compare against) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 644 Td (three baselines: translate-then-read, static embeddings and a cross-lingual) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 628 Td (transformer without the token scorer. All models share the same parameter budget and) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 612 Td (training schedule.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 72 596 Td (4.1 Results) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 560 Td (Our framework achieves an exact-match score of 61.3 on XQuAD-R and 58.9 on MLQA-R,) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 544 Td (outperforming the strongest baseline by 4.2 and 3.8 points respectively. The attention) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 528 Td (visualization shows that lower layers align tokens across languages, while upper) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 512 Td (layers focus on query-relevant content. Inference latency is 18 percent lower than the) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 496 Td (translate-then-read pipeline.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 72 480 Td (5. Conclusion) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 444 Td (We presented a cross-lingual attention framework that reads the source language) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 428 Td (directly and learns token-level alignment without translation. The approach improves) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 412 Td (accuracy on two benchmarks and reduces latency. Future work includes extending the) Tj ET
BT /F1 12.0 Tf 72 396 Td (framework to more language families and document-level tasks such as summarization.) Tj ET
